Survey.prompt:
Run the cheap survey for performance pathology.

Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Scope filter: ${vars.scope_filter}
Hot paths: ${vars.hot_paths}
Operator hints: ${vars.operator_hints}
Baseline / runtime evidence refs: ${vars.baseline_refs}
Target context window: ${vars.target_context_window}
Whiteboard id: ${vars.whiteboard_id}

Use cheap measurement before LLM judgment: bbox_code_symbols and bbox_refactor_status over hot_paths/scope_filter, bbox_code_refs / bbox_code_query / bbox_code_usages to find loops, fetch sites, async awaits, growing containers, and serialization round-trips, and bbox_hybrid_search/bbox_search/bbox_notes for prior performance pressure when hints or history point there. Read the baseline_refs (profiles, query logs, benchmarks, metrics) where present — runtime corroboration is the strongest signal. Do not run every atom. Select a bounded top set of atom requests whose diagnostic question is justified by the survey; strongly prefer cost centers with runtime corroboration or unambiguous hot-path context, and always include perf-runtime-evidence-corroboration when baseline_refs is non-empty.

Return strict JSON only with keys: survey_summary, cost_map, hot_paths, atom_requests, deferred_hotspots, limits. atom_requests must be an array of objects shaped {"atom_ref":"atom:perf-n-plus-one-fetch@v1","args":{...}}. Each args object must include project_dir, scope_filter, hot_paths, operator_hints, baseline_refs, survey_json, target_context_window, and whiteboard_id. Use only these atom refs: atom:perf-nested-iteration-complexity@v1, atom:perf-eager-materialization@v1, atom:perf-n-plus-one-fetch@v1, atom:perf-blocking-and-sequential-async@v1, atom:perf-unbounded-growth@v1, atom:perf-runtime-evidence-corroboration@v1. If evidence is weak, return fewer atom_requests and explain the limit. First byte {, final byte }.

Review.prompt:
Review and synthesize the focused atom outputs for performance pathology.

Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Scope: ${vars.scope_filter}
Whiteboard id: ${vars.whiteboard_id}
Survey JSON: ${vars.survey_json}
Atom result collection: ${vars.atom_results}

Post whiteboard_post entries for surviving cost-center claims, concerns about uncorroborated static-only smells, expected-improvement uncertainty, and merged diagnoses. Use agent_name="pathologist" for every whiteboard call; the setup node registered that identity as facilitator. Reject micro-optimization noise, compiler/lint-shaped findings, duplicate claims, and any static-only candidate that the perf-runtime-evidence-corroboration atom refuted or could not promote AND whose hot-path context is ambiguous. Prefer candidates with runtime corroboration. Distinguish observed cost from possible cost in every surviving claim. Do not transition the board; the workflow advances phases after your JSON parses.

Return strict JSON only with keys: surviving_diagnoses, rejected_or_deferred, merged_claims, baseline, expected_improvement, verification_costs, whiteboard_summary. First byte {, final byte }.

SynthesizePlan.prompt:
Write the reviewed Performance Correction Plan payload as strict JSON. Do not write files; the workflow writes markdown after parsing your JSON.

Project: ${vars.project_dir}
Scope: ${vars.scope_filter}
Baseline commit stdout: ${vars.baseline_result.stdout}
Target context window: ${vars.target_context_window}
Survey JSON: ${vars.survey_json}
Atom results: ${vars.atom_results}
Review JSON: ${vars.review_json}

The correction plan must have concrete evidence (static code refs plus any runtime evidence), a Baseline statement (measurements + method, or an explicit advisory note that baseline capture is the first slice), ordered bounded remediation slices ranked by expected benefit/risk, expected improvement per slice, and delta-based PD-ready acceptance criteria with PP-* ids stating their verification method (per-slice benchmark, query-log replay, profile recapture, or manual). Deferred must hold rejected/speculative/static-only-uncorroborated candidates. The plan must be explicitly usable as input to phase-decompose-main-edit. Distinguish observed cost from possible cost.

Return strict JSON only with keys: slug, title, brief, diagnosis_summary, evidence, authority_grades, atom_mapping, remediation_plan, acceptance_criteria, deferred. The 'evidence' string should include a '### Baseline' subsection. Markdown strings are allowed in diagnosis_summary/evidence/authority_grades/atom_mapping/remediation_plan/deferred. First byte {, final byte }.
